  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development by virtue of its substandard floorspace, bedroom size and layout would represent a substandard and inappropriate form of accommodation which would not be capable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers and would be detrimental to the residential amenities of future occupants. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP4 of the Enfield Plan Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD5, DMD8 and DMD37 of the Development Management Document (2014), the Mayor of London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance, The Technical Housing Standards-Nationally Described Space Standards and the guidance contained within the National Planning Policy Framework (2024).",
    "The site falls within Flood Zone 2 and insufficient information has been submitted to appropriately consider and mitigate the risks of flooding / surface water from all possible sources and allow for adequate measures to make the proposed development safe over its lifetime. Therefore, the proposal is not compliant with the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF, 2024), Policies SI 12 and SI 13 of the London Plan (2021), DMD 59, DMD 60, DMD 61, DMD 62 and DMD 63 of the Development Management Document (2014) and CP21, CP28 and CP29 of the Core Strategy (2010).",
    "The proposed first floor rear access over the flat roof, by reason of its siting, scale, and relationship with neighbouring properties, would result in an elevated external area that enables direct and prolonged overlooking into neighbouring gardens and habitable rooms, along Park Avenue. The development would result in an unneighbourly form of development, causing an unacceptable loss of privacy and residential amenity, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D4 of the London Plan (2021), Policies DMD 8, DMD 9, and DMD 37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and Core Policy 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010)."
  ],
